          'Molar mass 2 g/mol. At a given temperature every gas has the same average kinetic energy, so the lightest molecules must have the highest speeds (about 1900 m/s at 25 °C). ' +
          'That is why H₂ invades the O₂ bulb first and in larger numbers.');
      } else {
        showPopup('Oxygen molecule (O₂)',
          'Molar mass 32 g/mol — sixteen times heavier than H₂. Equal kinetic energy with sixteen times the mass means about one-quarter the average speed (≈480 m/s at 25 °C), ' +
